A branch that opens onto nothing reads as broken
==============================================

Clicking Projects opened the row and showed an empty space, because there were no projects stored —
the same failure as Tools & skills before it listed connections. An expansion has to resolve to
something or the control is lying about what it does.

Every group now yields at least one row. With nothing stored it says so and takes you to the page that
creates one: "No projects yet", "No artifacts yet", "No cron jobs yet", "No connections yet". Tools &
skills keeps listing configured connections first, because those exist by the time the sidebar draws
while the skill index does not.

